WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.397
Welcome to the Oribrix Vendor Portal course. Module one.

2
00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:06.581
A full tour of the vendor console.

3
00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:14.033
In the first course you learned how a vendor applies, and how the admin approves the

4
00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:18.108
KYC. This course starts right after that. The vendor is approved.

5
00:00:18.108 --> 00:00:21.055
Now what does the vendor actually do every day?

6
00:00:21.505 --> 00:00:23.852
First, where exactly this course begins.

7
00:00:24.302 --> 00:00:28.120
Then the ten sections you see on the left side of the vendor console.

8
00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.536
Then how to read the dashboard, with its four key numbers.

9
00:00:31.986 --> 00:00:34.695
Then the words you will hear again and again in this course.

10
00:00:35.145 --> 00:00:37.428
And finally, who is allowed to do what.

11
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:43.956
Here is the vendor's full journey. The first two steps were covered in the

12
00:00:43.956 --> 00:00:47.300
Onboarding course. This course covers everything after that.

13
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.990
The vendor applied to sell on Oribrix.

14
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.173
The admin checked the documents, and the KYC is approved.

15
00:00:54.623 --> 00:00:58.655
Now the vendor adds a warehouse, which is the place goods are picked up from.

16
00:00:59.105 --> 00:01:03.948
Then the vendor adds SKUs, which means stock of products from the master catalog.

17
00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:08.536
Customers order, and the vendor accepts, packs and hands over the order.

18
00:01:08.986 --> 00:01:12.081
And at the end, the vendor gets paid through settlements.

19
00:01:12.081 --> 00:01:14.469
We'll cover each of these in its own module.

20
00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:22.362
This is the left menu of the vendor console. It is grouped into overview, inventory,

21
00:01:22.362 --> 00:01:26.680
Orders and dispatch, finance, warehouses and returns, and account.

22
00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:31.610
Dashboard is the home page. It shows orders, sales and live activity.

23
00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:37.479
Inventory is where the vendor adds SKUs, updates stock and requests price changes.

24
00:01:37.929 --> 00:01:42.046
Orders is where new orders are accepted, picked, packed and dispatched.

25
00:01:42.496 --> 00:01:47.040
E-Way Bills is for high value orders, fifty thousand rupees and above.

26
00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:51.608
Drivers and Fleet is for the vendor's own local drivers and vehicles.

27
00:01:52.058 --> 00:01:56.068
Earnings and Settlements shows payouts, deductions and the Tally export.

28
00:01:56.518 --> 00:01:59.633
Warehouses lists every pickup location of the vendor.

29
00:02:00.083 --> 00:02:04.158
Returns and Disputes shows customer return requests and their status.

30
00:02:04.608 --> 00:02:09.152
KYC shows the approved business details. These are read only now.

31
00:02:09.602 --> 00:02:13.954
And Settings has password reset, staff accounts, and privacy and data.

32
00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:21.167
Let's open the dashboard. This is the first screen a vendor sees after logging in.

33
00:02:21.617 --> 00:02:24.902
Orders. The total number of orders in the selected period.

34
00:02:25.352 --> 00:02:30.961
G M V, gross merchandise value. The total value of everything sold, before any

35
00:02:30.961 --> 00:02:31.752
Deductions.

36
00:02:32.202 --> 00:02:36.511
S L A rate. The percentage of orders handled within the promised time.

37
00:02:36.511 --> 00:02:37.557
Higher is better.

38
00:02:38.007 --> 00:02:42.999
A O V, average order value. G M V divided by the number of orders.

39
00:02:43.449 --> 00:02:48.644
This chart shows revenue and orders day by day, so the vendor can see busy and quiet

40
00:02:48.644 --> 00:02:48.953
Days.

41
00:02:49.403 --> 00:02:54.513
And live activity shows the latest events, like a new order with its order I D and

42
00:02:54.513 --> 00:02:54.950
Amount.

43
00:02:57.333 --> 00:02:59.253
Let's watch this in the live demo.

44
00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:04.634
This is the vendor dashboard from the live session.

45
00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:07.882
At the top, a welcome message and the vendor's rating.

46
00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:14.192
Hovering on the chart shows the revenue and number of orders for that day.

47
00:03:23.867 --> 00:03:27.579
Below the chart, live activity lists new orders as they arrive.

48
00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:38.427
Scrolling down shows warehouse capacity and what needs action right now.

49
00:03:39.867 --> 00:03:44.308
From here the vendor moves to Inventory, which is where real work begins.

50
00:03:44.308 --> 00:03:46.011
We'll do that in module two.

51
00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.248
Before we go further, let's lock in some words.

52
00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:56.837
S K U, stock keeping unit. For a vendor, one S K U means one product, in one

53
00:03:56.837 --> 00:03:59.272
Warehouse, with its stock and price.

54
00:03:59.722 --> 00:04:04.489
Master catalog. The list of all products. Only the admin creates products.

55
00:04:04.489 --> 00:04:06.164
Vendors only pick from it.

56
00:04:06.614 --> 00:04:11.969
G M V. The total value sold, before commission, refunds or other deductions.

57
00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:16.152
S L A. The promised time within which an order must be handled.

58
00:04:16.602 --> 00:04:18.693
A O V. Average order value.

59
00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.831
A few more words, mostly about shipping and money.

60
00:04:24.281 --> 00:04:29.342
Shiprocket. Oribrix's main courier partner. It assigns a courier, picks up from the

61
00:04:29.342 --> 00:04:30.745
Warehouse and delivers.

62
00:04:31.195 --> 00:04:35.739
A W B, air waybill. The tracking number the courier gives to a shipment.

63
00:04:36.189 --> 00:04:41.208
E-way bill. A government transport document needed when goods worth fifty thousand

64
00:04:41.208 --> 00:04:42.738
Rupees or more are moved.

65
00:04:43.188 --> 00:04:48.052
Settlement. One payout cycle, where the vendor's earnings for a period are paid out.

66
00:04:48.502 --> 00:04:53.259
And Tally. The accounting software. Settlement data can be exported for Tally.

67
00:04:55.666 --> 00:04:58.717
Three kinds of people touch the vendor side of Oribrix.

68
00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:04.369
The vendor's main login does the daily work. Warehouses, S K Us, orders, e-way

69
00:05:04.369 --> 00:05:06.569
Bills, and creating staff logins.

70
00:05:07.019 --> 00:05:12.143
Vendor staff are sub logins. They see only the sections and warehouses the main

71
00:05:12.143 --> 00:05:15.062
Login allows. They cannot create other users.

72
00:05:15.512 --> 00:05:20.627
And the admin, which is the Oribrix team, approves warehouses, price and policy

73
00:05:20.627 --> 00:05:24.771
Changes, reviews e-way bills, and can suspend or block a vendor.

74
00:05:27.166 --> 00:05:31.893
Here is the golden rule of the vendor portal. The vendor proposes, the admin

75
00:05:31.893 --> 00:05:36.932
Approves. A new warehouse, a price change, a warranty or return policy change, an

76
00:05:36.932 --> 00:05:42.032
E-way bill. The vendor submits it, and nothing goes live until the admin approves.

77
00:05:42.032 --> 00:05:47.195
So when a vendor asks, why is my change not showing, the first question is: has the

78
00:05:47.195 --> 00:05:48.563
Admin approved it yet?

79
00:06:37.266 --> 00:06:42.110
Here's a quick preview of the inventory page, which we'll study in detail in module

80
00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:42.343
Two.

81
00:06:42.793 --> 00:06:46.164
Active S K Us. How many products this vendor is selling.

82
00:06:46.614 --> 00:06:50.006
Stock quantity. The total units across all S K Us.

83
00:06:50.456 --> 00:06:54.957
Stock status breakdown. How many are in stock, low, or out of stock.

84
00:06:55.407 --> 00:06:58.181
And the Add S K U button, which starts everything.

85
00:07:00.566 --> 00:07:04.193
And this is the orders page, which we'll cover in module four.

86
00:07:04.643 --> 00:07:08.461
Awaiting action. New orders that the vendor still has to accept.

87
00:07:08.911 --> 00:07:12.581
In fulfilment. Accepted orders that are being picked and packed.

88
00:07:13.031 --> 00:07:15.740
On the road. Orders that are out for delivery.

89
00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:20.947
And below, every order with its customer, warehouse, amount, payment and status.

90
00:07:23.333 --> 00:07:28.123
Let's follow one order from the customer to the vendor, so the sections make sense

91
00:07:28.123 --> 00:07:32.037
Together. Say a contractor in Lucknow orders twenty bags of cement.

92
00:07:32.487 --> 00:07:36.007
The contractor places the order in the Oribrix customer app.

93
00:07:36.457 --> 00:07:41.108
The system finds the nearest approved warehouse that has this product in stock.

94
00:07:41.558 --> 00:07:46.348
The vendor who owns that warehouse gets a sound and a pop-up alert on the vendor

95
00:07:46.348 --> 00:07:46.827
Console.

96
00:07:47.277 --> 00:07:49.986
The vendor checks the items and accepts the order.

97
00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:54.943
The vendor picks and packs the goods, and hands them over to Shiprocket or to a

98
00:07:54.943 --> 00:07:55.684
Local driver.

99
00:07:56.134 --> 00:08:00.685
The order is delivered, and the money reaches the vendor in the next settlement.

100
00:08:00.685 --> 00:08:03.814
Every one of these steps is a section in the left menu.

101
00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:10.447
If you support vendors, you will hear these five questions again and again.

102
00:08:10.447 --> 00:08:14.072
By the end of this course, you'll be able to answer all of them.

103
00:08:14.522 --> 00:08:19.786
Why can't customers see my product? Usually the warehouse is not approved, intake is

104
00:08:19.786 --> 00:08:21.541
Paused, or there's no stock.

105
00:08:21.991 --> 00:08:26.889
Why is my new warehouse still pending? Because the admin first verifies the pickup

106
00:08:26.889 --> 00:08:28.263
Address, then approves.

107
00:08:28.713 --> 00:08:33.297
Why didn't my price change apply? It is waiting for admin approval, or it was

108
00:08:33.297 --> 00:08:33.833
Rejected.

109
00:08:34.283 --> 00:08:37.522
I dismissed an alert, is the order cancelled? No.

110
00:08:37.522 --> 00:08:39.637
Dismiss only silences the alert.

111
00:08:40.087 --> 00:08:44.835
And why can't I add S K Us any more? The account may be suspended, which makes it

112
00:08:44.835 --> 00:08:45.421
Read only.

113
00:08:47.833 --> 00:08:51.332
Let's put it together. This is what a good vendor's day looks like.

114
00:08:51.782 --> 00:08:54.939
In the morning, open the dashboard and check live activity.

115
00:08:55.389 --> 00:08:59.848
Accept every new order quickly. A slow accept hurts the S L A rate.

116
00:09:00.298 --> 00:09:02.154
Pick, pack and hand over on time.

117
00:09:02.604 --> 00:09:06.444
For orders of fifty thousand rupees or more, upload the e-way bill.

118
00:09:06.894 --> 00:09:11.986
Keep stock numbers honest. If the app shows stock that isn't there, orders fail and

119
00:09:11.986 --> 00:09:13.336
Customers are unhappy.

120
00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:16.410
And once a week, check returns and settlements.

121
00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:23.756
Quick check. A vendor raised a price change yesterday, but customers still see the

122
00:09:23.756 --> 00:09:25.691
Old price. Why? Pause and think.

123
00:09:29.641 --> 00:09:34.547
The answer: the admin hasn't approved it yet. Vendor proposes, admin approves.

124
00:09:37.333 --> 00:09:39.061
Let's summarise module one.

125
00:09:39.511 --> 00:09:42.839
This course starts after the vendor's KYC is approved.

126
00:09:43.289 --> 00:09:46.532
The vendor console has ten sections in the left menu.

127
00:09:46.982 --> 00:09:51.056
The dashboard shows orders, G M V, S L A rate and A O V.

128
00:09:51.506 --> 00:09:54.557
Staff logins see only what the main login allows.

129
00:09:55.007 --> 00:09:58.483
And the golden rule: vendor proposes, admin approves.

130
00:09:58.483 --> 00:10:00.319
In module two, we add stock.

131
00:10:02.733 --> 00:10:08.941
That's the end of module 1. Next up, module 2: Inventory, SKUs and change requests.
